.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_WRITE 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_write \- write bytes through an MPQ file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_write("
.BI "        mpq_writer_s *" "writer,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "buffer,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Appends \fIsize\fP bytes from caller-owned \fIbuffer\fP to the active
\fIwriter\fP. The writer remains active on success. Bytes may be buffered
or written as complete sectors; call libmpq__writer_finish(3) to publish
the member entry.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP when the bytes are accepted, or a negative
libmpq error. This call does not consume the writer.
.SH ERRORS
A NULL writer, NULL data with nonzero size, negative size, or data beyond
the declared unpacked size returns \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP. Compression
and I/O errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_add_data (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_add_path (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_finish (3)
